@* The accountant navigation: the case list, the create page, and the existing
   sign-out as an antiforgery form.

   It is placed inside accountant pages and never in PortalLayout, which client
   pages share: a client response must carry no accountant link or control.

   Parameterless, statically server rendered, and it injects nothing. Every
   target is a fixed existing route; no identifier is rendered here. *@

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms

<nav class="actions" aria-label="Accountant">
    <a class="button-link" href="/intake-cases">Cases</a>
    <a class="button-link" href="/intake-cases/new">New case</a>
    <form method="post" action="/sign-out">
        <AntiforgeryToken />
        <button type="submit" class="secondary">Sign out</button>
    </form>
</nav>
